.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.In threads.h
header provides the ISO C11 threads interface.
It is a standardised interface over the
.Xr pthread 3
implementation that is part of
.Xr libc 3 ;
every object is a real pthread object underneath and no separate
synchronisation primitive is introduced.
.Pp
.Fn thrd_create
creates a thread that runs
.Fa func
with argument
.Fa arg .
.Fn thrd_join
waits for a thread to terminate and stores its result;
.Fn thrd_detach
releases the resources of a thread whose result is not needed.
.Fn thrd_exit
terminates the calling thread.
.Fn thrd_equal
compares two thread identifiers and
.Fn thrd_current
returns the identifier of the calling thread.
.Fn thrd_sleep
suspends the calling thread;
.Fn thrd_yield
offers the processor to another thread.
.Pp
.Fn mtx_init
initializes a mutex.
.Fa type
is
.Dv mtx_plain ,
.Dv mtx_recursive
or
.Dv mtx_timed ,
or the bitwise OR of
.Dv mtx_recursive
and
.Dv mtx_timed .
.Fn mtx_lock
blocks until the mutex is locked,
.Fn mtx_trylock
returns
.Dv thrd_busy
if the mutex is already locked,
and
.Fn mtx_timedlock
blocks until the absolute
.Fa ts
time.
.Pp
.Fn cnd_init
initializes a condition variable.
.Fn cnd_wait
and
.Fn cnd_timedwait
atomically release the mutex and wait for a signal;
.Fn cnd_timedwait
returns
.Dv thrd_timedout
when the absolute
.Fa ts
time passes.
.Fn cnd_signal
wakes one waiter and
.Fn cnd_broadcast
wakes all of them.
.Pp
.Fn tss_create
creates a thread-specific storage key with destructor
.Fa dtor ;
.Fn tss_get
and
.Fn tss_set
access the value associated with the calling thread.
.Pp
.Fn call_once
calls
.Fa func
exactly once for a given
.Fa flag .
A
.Vt once_flag
must be initialized with
.Dv ONCE_FLAG_INIT .
.Pp
The
.Dv thread_local
macro, available before ISO C23, is a synonym for
.Va _Thread_local .
.Sh RETURN VALUES
The functions that can fail return
.Dv thrd_success
on success and one of
.Dv thrd_timedout ,
.Dv thrd_busy ,
.Dv thrd_nomem
or
.Dv thrd_error
on failure.
.Fn thrd_join
stores the result of the thread in
.Fa res
when
.Fa res
is not
.Dv NULL .
.Fn thrd_sleep
returns 0 when the requested interval elapsed, \-1 when it was interrupted
and \-2 on error.
.Pp
.Fn thrd_yield ,
.Fn thrd_exit ,
.Fn mtx_destroy ,
.Fn cnd_destroy
and
.Fn tss_delete
return no value.
.Sh NOTES
The base clang currently predefines
.Dv __STDC_NO_THREADS__
when targeting
.Ox ,
because the base system has historically lacked
.In threads.h .
This interface is provided by libc nonetheless; including
.In threads.h
withdraws the stale macro, and the compiler's target description should be
updated to match.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr pthread 3 ,
.Xr stdatomic 3
.Sh STANDARDS
The
.In threads.h
header conforms to
.St -isoC-2011
and ISO/IEC 9899:2024 (C23).
.Sh HISTORY
The
.In threads.h
header appeared in
.Ox 8.0 .
